@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `law-commencement`
IMPORT `second-schedule`
IMPORT `law-licensing`
IMPORT `law-duties`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`

-- ===========================================================================
-- tests-law.l4 — the Law's sections 2, 3, 6 and the Second Schedule, 7, 8,
-- 9, 16, 17 and 63. Expected values are read off the Law's text, with the
-- date arithmetic done by hand from the dates the sources give: publication
-- 14 January 2025 (SH 3349) and the Fees Regulations in force 16 July 2025.
--
-- Since 2026-10-13 periods are counted by Interpretation Law s 10 (and "until"
-- by its s 8), through the vendored il-interpretation-time.l4. Every expectation
-- that moved, or was added, was decided from s 10 and the weekday of the day
-- in question, read off a calendar, before the modules were run; NOTES.md §11
-- lists each with its old and new value.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Tests — the Law`

§§ `Illustrative calendars of days of rest (Interpretation Law s 10(c))`

-- s 10(c) needs the days of rest, recess or holiday as an INPUT. These three
-- calendars are illustrations supplied by this file. They are not a statement
-- of any Israeli calendar, and they hold no holiday.
-- 2020-01-04 was a Saturday, so a day is a Saturday when its day count is a
-- multiple of seven from that one (the Interpretation row's own idiom).
`no days of rest` MEANS `days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` EMPTY

GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Saturdays are days of rest` day MEANS
    ((Day day MINUS Day (YMD 2020 1 4)) MODULO 7) EQUALS 0

GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest` day MEANS
    ((Day day MINUS Day (YMD 2020 1 4)) MODULO 7) EQUALS 0 OR ((Day day MINUS Day (YMD 2020 1 4)) MODULO 7) EQUALS 6

-- The calendars themselves, on days whose weekday was read off a calendar.
#ASSERT `Saturdays are days of rest` (YMD 2028 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Saturdays are days of rest` (YMD 2028 1 2)
#ASSERT `Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest` (YMD 2030 2 15)
#ASSERT NOT `Saturdays are days of rest` (YMD 2030 2 15)

§§ `Section 63 — commencement`

-- s 10(b): three months from 14.1.2025 end on 14.4.2025; the Regulations:
-- 16.7.2025; the later is 16.7.2025. Eighteen months from it end on 16.1.2027.
-- (Unchanged by the 2026-10-13 correction: `add months` already gave these.)
#ASSERT `three months from the day this Law was published` EQUALS YMD 2025 4 14
#ASSERT `the commencement day` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16
#ASSERT `eighteen months from the commencement day` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 16

-- Fork F31, made visible: 16.1.2027 is a Saturday. s 10(c) is NOT applied to a
-- commencement here; the reading that applies it would move (a)(2)'s day to
-- Sunday 17.1.2027 under a Saturday calendar, and not at all with no rest days.
#ASSERT `eighteen months from the commencement day, if s 10(c) applied to a commencement, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 16
#ASSERT `eighteen months from the commencement day, if s 10(c) applied to a commencement, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 17

`a 10 kW split system on a non-flammable refrigerant` MEANS
    System WITH
        `removes heat from a given material or space`              IS TRUE
        `does so by means of a refrigerant`                        IS TRUE
        `cooling capacity in kilowatts`                            IS 10
        `operates with a flammable refrigerant listed in the Fourth Schedule` IS FALSE
        `the use of that refrigerant is permitted by law`          IS TRUE
        `of a type exempted by an order under section 3(b)`        IS FALSE

`a 10 kW system on a listed flammable refrigerant permitted by law` MEANS
    System WITH
        `removes heat from a given material or space`              IS TRUE
        `does so by means of a refrigerant`                        IS TRUE
        `cooling capacity in kilowatts`                            IS 10
        `operates with a flammable refrigerant listed in the Fourth Schedule` IS TRUE
        `the use of that refrigerant is permitted by law`          IS TRUE
        `of a type exempted by an order under section 3(b)`        IS FALSE

`a 10 kW system on a listed flammable refrigerant not permitted by law` MEANS
    System WITH
        `removes heat from a given material or space`              IS TRUE
        `does so by means of a refrigerant`                        IS TRUE
        `cooling capacity in kilowatts`                            IS 10
        `operates with a flammable refrigerant listed in the Fourth Schedule` IS TRUE
        `the use of that refrigerant is permitted by law`          IS FALSE
        `of a type exempted by an order under section 3(b)`        IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the day this Law, other than Chapter F, comes into force for work on` `a 10 kW system on a listed flammable refrigerant permitted by law` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16
#ASSERT `the day this Law, other than Chapter F, comes into force for work on` `a 10 kW split system on a non-flammable refrigerant` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 16
#ASSERT `the day this Law, other than Chapter F, comes into force for work on` `a 10 kW system on a listed flammable refrigerant not permitted by law` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 16

-- (ב) Chapter F: the later of 16.1.2027 and the s. 46 regulations.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day Chapter F comes into force, given` NOTHING BECAUSE "the day regulations under section 46 came into force is not in the sources"
#ASSERT `the day Chapter F comes into force, given` (JUST (YMD 2027 3 1)) EQUALS YMD 2027 3 1
#ASSERT `the day Chapter F comes into force, given` (JUST (YMD 2026 1 1)) EQUALS YMD 2027 1 16

§§ `Section 2 — definitions`

#ASSERT `section 2 — a refrigeration or air-conditioning system` `a 10 kW split system on a non-flammable refrigerant`

`a fan that moves air without a refrigerant` MEANS
    System WITH
        `removes heat from a given material or space`              IS TRUE
        `does so by means of a refrigerant`                        IS FALSE
        `cooling capacity in kilowatts`                            IS 1
        `operates with a flammable refrigerant listed in the Fourth Schedule` IS FALSE
        `the use of that refrigerant is permitted by law`          IS FALSE
        `of a type exempted by an order under section 3(b)`        IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `section 2 — a refrigeration or air-conditioning system` `a fan that moves air without a refrigerant`

-- "עד 18" / "עד 70" include the figure; grade 3 covers every system.
#ASSERT `section 2 — a licence of` `grade 1` `covers a system whose cooling capacity in kilowatts is` 18
#ASSERT NOT `section 2 — a licence of` `grade 1` `covers a system whose cooling capacity in kilowatts is` 18.5
#ASSERT `section 2 — a licence of` `grade 2` `covers a system whose cooling capacity in kilowatts is` 70
#ASSERT NOT `section 2 — a licence of` `grade 2` `covers a system whose cooling capacity in kilowatts is` 70.1
#ASSERT `section 2 — a licence of` `grade 3` `covers a system whose cooling capacity in kilowatts is` 5000

-- "תעודת גמר" (1) needs an exam that included BOTH a theoretical and a
-- practical exam.
`a Division certificate after a theoretical and a practical exam` MEANS
    `Certificate as issued` WITH
        `issued by`                                                       IS `the Division for vocational training`
        `attests completion of refrigeration and air-conditioning studies` IS TRUE
        `attests passing an exam the Division conducted`                  IS TRUE
        `that exam included a theoretical exam`                           IS TRUE
        `that exam included a practical exam`                             IS TRUE
        `attests successful completion of studies in the climate-control track` IS FALSE

`a Division certificate after a practical exam only` MEANS
    `Certificate as issued` WITH
        `issued by`                                                       IS `the Division for vocational training`
        `attests completion of refrigeration and air-conditioning studies` IS TRUE
        `attests passing an exam the Division conducted`                  IS TRUE
        `that exam included a theoretical exam`                           IS FALSE
        `that exam included a practical exam`                             IS TRUE
        `attests successful completion of studies in the climate-control track` IS FALSE

`a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate` MEANS
    `Certificate as issued` WITH
        `issued by`                                                       IS `the Ministry of Education`
        `attests completion of refrigeration and air-conditioning studies` IS FALSE
        `attests passing an exam the Division conducted`                  IS FALSE
        `that exam included a theoretical exam`                           IS FALSE
        `that exam included a practical exam`                             IS FALSE
        `attests successful completion of studies in the climate-control track` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `section 2 — a completion certificate` `a Division certificate after a theoretical and a practical exam`
#ASSERT NOT `section 2 — a completion certificate` `a Division certificate after a practical exam only`
#ASSERT `section 2 — a completion certificate` `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate`

§§ `Section 8 — the validity period`

-- The five years end, by Interpretation Law s 10(b), ON the fifth anniversary;
-- "עד 31 במרץ" includes 31 March (Interpretation Law s 8).
-- Granted 16.7.2025: five years end 16.7.2030; 31.3.2030 is earlier.
#ASSERT `section 8 — the last day of the validity period of a licence granted or renewed on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2030 3 31
-- Granted 15.2.2025: five years end 15.2.2030 (was 14.2.2030 before the
-- s 10 correction), earlier than 31.3.2030.
#ASSERT `section 8 — the last day of the validity period of a licence granted or renewed on` (YMD 2025 2 15) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2030 2 15
-- Granted 31.3.2025: the five years and 31 March both end on 31.3.2030 (was
-- 30.3.2030).
#ASSERT `section 8 — the last day of the validity period of a licence granted or renewed on` (YMD 2025 3 31) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2030 3 31
-- Granted 1.4.2025: the five years end 1.4.2030; 31.3.2030 is earlier.
#ASSERT `section 8 — the last day of the validity period of a licence granted or renewed on` (YMD 2025 4 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2030 3 31

-- s 10(c), applied to a period of validity (fork F31).
-- Granted 15.2.2025: the anniversary 15.2.2030 is a Friday. Saturdays only: it
-- stands. Fridays and Saturdays: Friday 15 and Saturday 16 are rest days, so
-- the five years run to Sunday 17.2.2030, still before 31 March.
#ASSERT `section 8 — the last day of the validity period of a licence granted or renewed on` (YMD 2025 2 15) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2030 2 15
#ASSERT `section 8 — the last day of the validity period of a licence granted or renewed on` (YMD 2025 2 15) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2030 2 17
-- Granted 30.3.2025: the anniversary 30.3.2030 is a Saturday. With no rest
-- days the licence ends that Saturday; with Saturdays as rest days the five
-- years run to Sunday 31.3.2030, which is also 31 March: 31.3.2030.
#ASSERT `section 8 — the last day of the validity period of a licence granted or renewed on` (YMD 2025 3 30) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2030 3 30
#ASSERT `section 8 — the last day of the validity period of a licence granted or renewed on` (YMD 2025 3 30) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2030 3 31
-- s 10(c) does not move the fixed day 31 March: with 30 and 31 March 2030 both
-- listed as holidays, the five years run to 1.4.2030, and 31.3.2030 is earlier.
#ASSERT `section 8 — the last day of the validity period of a licence granted or renewed on` (YMD 2025 3 30) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (LIST YMD 2030 3 30, YMD 2030 3 31)) EQUALS YMD 2030 3 31

§§ `Section 6 and the Second Schedule — who may be granted which licence`

GIVEN quals IS A LIST OF Qualification
GIVETH AN Applicant
`an adult Israeli citizen with no disqualifying offence, with` quals MEANS
    Applicant WITH
        `of full age`                         IS TRUE
        `an Israeli citizen`                  IS TRUE
        `a resident of Israel`                IS TRUE
        `convicted of, or under a pending indictment for, an offence that in the Registrar's opinion makes the applicant unfit to hold a licence` IS FALSE
        `prior training, experience and completed studies` IS quals
        `holds a valid electricity licence listed in paragraphs (1) to (7) of regulation 7 of the Electricity (Licences) Regulations 5745-1985` IS FALSE
        `holds a valid work-at-height approval under regulations 5 and 6 of the Work Safety (Work at Height) Regulations 5767-2007` IS FALSE

`a graduate of the Division's 350-hour grade 1 course` MEANS
    `an adult Israeli citizen with no disqualifying offence, with` (LIST `completion of the Division's training of up to` 350 `the Division's grade 1 certificate`)

`a worker with a year's experience and the 220-hour grade 1 course` MEANS
    `an adult Israeli citizen with no disqualifying offence, with` (LIST `one year of cumulative experience within the three years before the licence application`, `completion of the Division's training of up to` 220 `the Division's grade 1 certificate`)

`a worker with a year's experience and the 350-hour grade 1 course` MEANS
    `an adult Israeli citizen with no disqualifying offence, with` (LIST `one year of cumulative experience within the three years before the licence application`, `completion of the Division's training of up to` 350 `the Division's grade 1 certificate`)

`a holder of the 3-unit Ministry of Education certificate` MEANS
    `an adult Israeli citizen with no disqualifying offence, with` (LIST `holding` `a Ministry of Education completion certificate in climate-control studies at 3 study units`)

`a registered certified technician who completed a programme with the supplementary course` MEANS
    `an adult Israeli citizen with no disqualifying offence, with` (LIST `registration as a certified technician in the refrigeration and air-conditioning branch and section`, `completion of a study programme that includes the supplementary course`)

`a registered certified technician without the supplementary course` MEANS
    `an adult Israeli citizen with no disqualifying offence, with` (LIST `registration as a certified technician in the refrigeration and air-conditioning branch and section`)

`a registered practical engineer who completed a programme with the supplementary course` MEANS
    `an adult Israeli citizen with no disqualifying offence, with` (LIST `registration as a practical engineer in the refrigeration and air-conditioning branch and section`, `completion of a study programme that includes the supplementary course`)

`a grade 2 licence holder who completed the 240-hour grade 3 course` MEANS
    `an adult Israeli citizen with no disqualifying offence, with` (LIST `a licence of` `grade 2`, `completion of the Division's training of up to` 240 `the Division's grade 3 certificate`)

`a holder of the Division's general certificate, with no further course` MEANS
    `an adult Israeli citizen with no disqualifying offence, with` (LIST `holding` `the Division's general completion certificate`)

`a holder of the Division's general certificate who completed the 50-hour course` MEANS
    `an adult Israeli citizen with no disqualifying offence, with` (LIST `holding` `the Division's general completion certificate`, `completion of the Division's training of up to` 50 `the Division's general completion certificate`)

`a mechanical engineer who completed the 230-hour grade 3 course` MEANS
    `an adult Israeli citizen with no disqualifying offence, with` (LIST `registration as an engineer in the mechanical branch under the Engineers and Architects Law 5718-1958`, `completion of the Division's training of up to` 230 `the Division's grade 3 certificate`)

`a minor who completed the 350-hour grade 1 course` MEANS
    Applicant WITH
        `of full age`                         IS FALSE
        `an Israeli citizen`                  IS TRUE
        `a resident of Israel`                IS TRUE
        `convicted of, or under a pending indictment for, an offence that in the Registrar's opinion makes the applicant unfit to hold a licence` IS FALSE
        `prior training, experience and completed studies` IS LIST `completion of the Division's training of up to` 350 `the Division's grade 1 certificate`
        `holds a valid electricity licence listed in paragraphs (1) to (7) of regulation 7 of the Electricity (Licences) Regulations 5745-1985` IS TRUE
        `holds a valid work-at-height approval under regulations 5 and 6 of the Work Safety (Work at Height) Regulations 5767-2007` IS FALSE

`a resident who is not a citizen, with the 350-hour grade 1 course` MEANS
    Applicant WITH
        `of full age`                         IS TRUE
        `an Israeli citizen`                  IS FALSE
        `a resident of Israel`                IS TRUE
        `convicted of, or under a pending indictment for, an offence that in the Registrar's opinion makes the applicant unfit to hold a licence` IS FALSE
        `prior training, experience and completed studies` IS LIST `completion of the Division's training of up to` 350 `the Division's grade 1 certificate`
        `holds a valid electricity licence listed in paragraphs (1) to (7) of regulation 7 of the Electricity (Licences) Regulations 5745-1985` IS FALSE
        `holds a valid work-at-height approval under regulations 5 and 6 of the Work Safety (Work at Height) Regulations 5767-2007` IS TRUE

`an applicant the Registrar found unfit, with the 350-hour grade 1 course` MEANS
    Applicant WITH
        `of full age`                         IS TRUE
        `an Israeli citizen`                  IS TRUE
        `a resident of Israel`                IS TRUE
        `convicted of, or under a pending indictment for, an offence that in the Registrar's opinion makes the applicant unfit to hold a licence` IS TRUE
        `prior training, experience and completed studies` IS LIST `completion of the Division's training of up to` 350 `the Division's grade 1 certificate`
        `holds a valid electricity licence listed in paragraphs (1) to (7) of regulation 7 of the Electricity (Licences) Regulations 5745-1985` IS FALSE
        `holds a valid work-at-height approval under regulations 5 and 6 of the Work Safety (Work at Height) Regulations 5767-2007` IS FALSE

-- Part A item 1: grade 1, but not grade 2.
#ASSERT `section 6(a) — the applicant meets every condition for a licence of` `a graduate of the Division's 350-hour grade 1 course` `grade 1` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `section 6(a) — the applicant meets every condition for a licence of` `a graduate of the Division's 350-hour grade 1 course` `grade 2` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1)
-- Part A item 2 and its three-year life. Three years from 16.7.2025 end, by
-- Interpretation Law s 10(b), on 16.7.2028, which is INSIDE the period: in
-- force on 16.7.2028 (before the correction, gone that day), gone on 17.7.2028.
#ASSERT `the last day of the three-year items of the Second Schedule` EQUALS YMD 2028 7 16
#ASSERT `section 6(a) — the applicant meets every condition for a licence of` `a worker with a year's experience and the 220-hour grade 1 course` `grade 1` `on` (YMD 2028 7 15)
#ASSERT `section 6(a) — the applicant meets every condition for a licence of` `a worker with a year's experience and the 220-hour grade 1 course` `grade 1` `on` (YMD 2028 7 16)
#ASSERT NOT `section 6(a) — the applicant meets every condition for a licence of` `a worker with a year's experience and the 220-hour grade 1 course` `grade 1` `on` (YMD 2028 7 17)
#ASSERT `the items of the Second Schedule open to` `a worker with a year's experience and the 220-hour grade 1 course` `for a licence of` `grade 1` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS LIST 1, 2
#ASSERT `the items of the Second Schedule open to` `a worker with a year's experience and the 220-hour grade 1 course` `for a licence of` `grade 1` `on` (YMD 2028 7 16) EQUALS LIST 1, 2
#ASSERT `the items of the Second Schedule open to` `a worker with a year's experience and the 220-hour grade 1 course` `for a licence of` `grade 1` `on` (YMD 2028 7 17) EQUALS LIST 1
-- The route "בלא הכשרה או ניסיון קודמים" is open to the experienced too (F13),
-- also after item 2 has lapsed (the day moved from 16.7.2028 to 17.7.2028 so
-- that item 2 is still gone, which is what this case is about).
#ASSERT `section 6(a) — the applicant meets every condition for a licence of` `a worker with a year's experience and the 350-hour grade 1 course` `grade 1` `on` (YMD 2028 7 17)
-- Part A item 1(2): the 3-unit Ministry of Education certificate is enough
-- for grade 1; for grade 2 it opens only item 3, the 100-hour course.
#ASSERT `section 6(a) — the applicant meets every condition for a licence of` `a holder of the 3-unit Ministry of Education certificate` `grade 1` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `section 6(a) — the applicant meets every condition for a licence of` `a holder of the 3-unit Ministry of Education certificate` `grade 2` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT `the items of the Second Schedule open to` `a holder of the 3-unit Ministry of Education certificate` `for a licence of` `grade 2` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS LIST 1, 3
-- Part B item 2: "בלא דרישות נוספות"; without the supplementary course, item 6's
-- 50-hour course is needed.
#ASSERT `section 6(a) — the applicant meets every condition for a licence of` `a registered certified technician who completed a programme with the supplementary course` `grade 2` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `section 6(a) — the applicant meets every condition for a licence of` `a registered certified technician who completed a programme with the supplementary course` `grade 3` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `section 6(a) — the applicant meets every condition for a licence of` `a registered certified technician without the supplementary course` `grade 2` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT `the items of the Second Schedule open to` `a registered certified technician without the supplementary course` `for a licence of` `grade 2` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS LIST 1, 6
-- Part C item 2.
#ASSERT `section 6(a) — the applicant meets every condition for a licence of` `a registered practical engineer who completed a programme with the supplementary course` `grade 3` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1)
-- Part C item 4, the row the wiki misprints: 240 hours is column B.
#ASSERT `section 6(a) — the applicant meets every condition for a licence of` `a grade 2 licence holder who completed the 240-hour grade 3 course` `grade 3` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1)
-- Part A item 3: the general certificate alone is not enough; with the
-- 50-hour course it is.
#ASSERT NOT `section 6(a) — the applicant meets every condition for a licence of` `a holder of the Division's general certificate, with no further course` `grade 1` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT `section 6(a) — the applicant meets every condition for a licence of` `a holder of the Division's general certificate who completed the 50-hour course` `grade 1` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1)
-- Part C item 8.
#ASSERT `section 6(a) — the applicant meets every condition for a licence of` `a mechanical engineer who completed the 230-hour grade 3 course` `grade 3` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1)
-- (1), (2), (3).
#ASSERT NOT `section 6(a) — the applicant meets every condition for a licence of` `a minor who completed the 350-hour grade 1 course` `grade 1` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT `section 6(a) — the applicant meets every condition for a licence of` `a resident who is not a citizen, with the 350-hour grade 1 course` `grade 1` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `section 6(a) — the applicant meets every condition for a licence of` `an applicant the Registrar found unfit, with the 350-hour grade 1 course` `grade 1` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1)

-- s. 6(a)'s duty, traced: the Registrar grants on day 10 → FULFILLED.
#TRACE `section 6(a) — the Registrar shall grant the licence` `a graduate of the Division's 350-hour grade 1 course` `grade 1` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `grant the licence` AT 10

§§ `Section 8 — renewal`

-- Renewal needs s. 6(a)(1)-(3) but not (4): an applicant with no training at
-- all may renew, but could not be granted a first licence.
`an adult citizen with no qualifications` MEANS
    `an adult Israeli citizen with no disqualifying offence, with` (EMPTY)

#ASSERT `section 8 — the licence may be renewed for a further validity period for` `an adult citizen with no qualifications`
#ASSERT NOT `section 6(a) — the applicant meets every condition for a licence of` `an adult citizen with no qualifications` `grade 1` `on` (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `section 8 — the licence may be renewed for a further validity period for` `a minor who completed the 350-hour grade 1 course`

§§ `Section 7 — exemption from training`

#ASSERT `section 7(a) — the Director may exempt from the electricity chapter of the training` `a minor who completed the 350-hour grade 1 course`
#ASSERT NOT `section 7(a) — the Director may exempt from the electricity chapter of the training` `a graduate of the Division's 350-hour grade 1 course`
#ASSERT `section 7(b) — the Director may exempt from the work-at-height chapter of the training` `a resident who is not a citizen, with the 350-hour grade 1 course`
#ASSERT NOT `section 7(b) — the Director may exempt from the work-at-height chapter of the training` `a graduate of the Division's 350-hour grade 1 course`

§§ `Section 9 — a temporary licence for a foreign expert`

`an expert invited for a 71 kW system` MEANS
    `Foreign applicant` WITH
        `from a foreign state`                                              IS TRUE
        `invited to Israel to work on a system whose cooling capacity, in kilowatts, is` IS 71
        `authorised to work on refrigeration or air-conditioning systems in a foreign state` IS TRUE
        `installed or maintained similar systems in the six years before the application` IS TRUE
        `recognised by the Registrar as having a reputation and as a renowned expert in the field` IS TRUE

`an expert invited for a 70 kW system` MEANS
    `Foreign applicant` WITH
        `from a foreign state`                                              IS TRUE
        `invited to Israel to work on a system whose cooling capacity, in kilowatts, is` IS 70
        `authorised to work on refrigeration or air-conditioning systems in a foreign state` IS TRUE
        `installed or maintained similar systems in the six years before the application` IS TRUE
        `recognised by the Registrar as having a reputation and as a renowned expert in the field` IS TRUE

`an unrecognised expert invited for a 200 kW system` MEANS
    `Foreign applicant` WITH
        `from a foreign state`                                              IS TRUE
        `invited to Israel to work on a system whose cooling capacity, in kilowatts, is` IS 200
        `authorised to work on refrigeration or air-conditioning systems in a foreign state` IS TRUE
        `installed or maintained similar systems in the six years before the application` IS TRUE
        `recognised by the Registrar as having a reputation and as a renowned expert in the field` IS FALSE

-- "מעל 70": 71 qualifies, 70 does not.
#ASSERT `section 9(a) — a foreign expert` `an expert invited for a 71 kW system`
#ASSERT NOT `section 9(a) — a foreign expert` `an expert invited for a 70 kW system`
#ASSERT NOT `section 9(a) — a foreign expert` `an unrecognised expert invited for a 200 kW system`

-- The SimpLEX worked example says "סעיף 9(א): מחייב מעבר בחינה" (requires
-- passing an exam). Section 9(a) as enacted names no exam: the 71 kW expert
-- above qualifies with no exam anywhere in the record. The exam requirement
-- the Law does have is in s. 2's "תעודת גמר" (tested above).

-- "לתקופה שלא תעלה על שנה". A year after 1.1.2027 ends, by Interpretation Law
-- s 10(b), on 1.1.2028, inside it (before the correction, that day was
-- outside). 1.1.2028 is a Saturday: with Saturdays (or Fridays and Saturdays)
-- as rest days, s 10(c) runs the year on to Sunday 2.1.2028 (fork F31).
#ASSERT `section 9 — a period from` (YMD 2027 1 1) `to` (YMD 2027 12 31) `does not exceed a year, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT `section 9 — a period from` (YMD 2027 1 1) `to` (YMD 2028 1 1) `does not exceed a year, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `section 9 — a period from` (YMD 2027 1 1) `to` (YMD 2028 1 2) `does not exceed a year, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT `section 9 — a period from` (YMD 2027 1 1) `to` (YMD 2028 1 2) `does not exceed a year, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest`
#ASSERT `section 9 — a period from` (YMD 2027 1 1) `to` (YMD 2028 1 2) `does not exceed a year, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `section 9 — a period from` (YMD 2027 1 1) `to` (YMD 2028 1 3) `does not exceed a year, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest`
-- (ב): two further periods.
#ASSERT `section 9(b) — the Registrar may renew a temporary licence already renewed this many times` 1
#ASSERT NOT `section 9(b) — the Registrar may renew a temporary licence already renewed this many times` 2

`a temporary grade 3 licence from 1.1.2027 to 31.12.2027` MEANS
    Licence WITH
        `the grade`                                  IS `grade 3`
        `temporary, for a foreign expert, under section 9` IS TRUE
        `the day it was granted or last renewed`     IS YMD 2027 1 1
        `the last day of the period the Registrar set, for a temporary licence` IS JUST (YMD 2027 12 31)
        `cancelled or suspended under section 10`    IS FALSE
        `the work is in accordance with the conditions of the licence and the provisions under this Law` IS TRUE

`a temporary grade 3 licence with no period given` MEANS
    Licence WITH
        `the grade`                                  IS `grade 3`
        `temporary, for a foreign expert, under section 9` IS TRUE
        `the day it was granted or last renewed`     IS YMD 2027 1 1
        `the last day of the period the Registrar set, for a temporary licence` IS NOTHING
        `cancelled or suspended under section 10`    IS FALSE
        `the work is in accordance with the conditions of the licence and the provisions under this Law` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the licence` `a temporary grade 3 licence from 1.1.2027 to 31.12.2027` `is in force on` (YMD 2027 12 31) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `the licence` `a temporary grade 3 licence from 1.1.2027 to 31.12.2027` `is in force on` (YMD 2028 1 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the licence` `a temporary grade 3 licence with no period given` `is in force on` (YMD 2027 6 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest` BECAUSE "the period the Registrar set for the temporary licence was not given"

§§ `Section 3 — the duty to hold a licence`

GIVEN g IS A `Licence grade`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Person doing the work`
`a holder of a` g `licence granted on` d MEANS
    `Person doing the work` WITH
        `the licence held` IS JUST (Licence WITH
            `the grade`                                  IS g
            `temporary, for a foreign expert, under section 9` IS FALSE
            `the day it was granted or last renewed`     IS d
            `the last day of the period the Registrar set, for a temporary licence` IS NOTHING
            `cancelled or suspended under section 10`    IS FALSE
            `the work is in accordance with the conditions of the licence and the provisions under this Law` IS TRUE)

`a person with no licence` MEANS
    `Person doing the work` WITH `the licence held` IS NOTHING

GIVEN s          IS A System
      `column A` IS A LIST OF `Licence grade`
      d          IS A DATE
GIVETH A Work
`work on` s `that the First Schedule sets against` `column A` `, done on` d MEANS
    Work WITH
        `the system worked on` IS s
        `an action of a type set out in the First Schedule` IS TRUE
        `the licence types column A of the First Schedule sets against this work` IS `column A`
        `the day the work is done` IS d

`a 20 kW system on a non-flammable refrigerant` MEANS
    System WITH
        `removes heat from a given material or space`              IS TRUE
        `does so by means of a refrigerant`                        IS TRUE
        `cooling capacity in kilowatts`                            IS 20
        `operates with a flammable refrigerant listed in the Fourth Schedule` IS FALSE
        `the use of that refrigerant is permitted by law`          IS TRUE
        `of a type exempted by an order under section 3(b)`        IS FALSE

`a 10 kW system of a type exempted by order` MEANS
    System WITH
        `removes heat from a given material or space`              IS TRUE
        `does so by means of a refrigerant`                        IS TRUE
        `cooling capacity in kilowatts`                            IS 10
        `operates with a flammable refrigerant listed in the Fourth Schedule` IS FALSE
        `the use of that refrigerant is permitted by law`          IS TRUE
        `of a type exempted by an order under section 3(b)`        IS TRUE

`every grade` MEANS LIST `grade 1`, `grade 2`, `grade 3`

-- No licence: not yet prohibited on 15.1.2027, prohibited from 16.1.2027
-- (s. 63(a)(2)); from 16.7.2025 on a listed flammable refrigerant (s. 63(a)(1)).
#ASSERT NOT `section 3 prohibits the work` `a person with no licence` (`work on` `a 10 kW split system on a non-flammable refrigerant` `that the First Schedule sets against` `every grade` `, done on` (YMD 2027 1 15)) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT `section 3 prohibits the work` `a person with no licence` (`work on` `a 10 kW split system on a non-flammable refrigerant` `that the First Schedule sets against` `every grade` `, done on` (YMD 2027 1 16)) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT `section 3 prohibits the work` `a person with no licence` (`work on` `a 10 kW system on a listed flammable refrigerant permitted by law` `that the First Schedule sets against` `every grade` `, done on` (YMD 2025 7 16)) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
-- A grade 1 licence does not cover 20 kW; a grade 2 does.
#ASSERT `section 3 prohibits the work` (`a holder of a` `grade 1` `licence granted on` (YMD 2026 10 1)) (`work on` `a 20 kW system on a non-flammable refrigerant` `that the First Schedule sets against` `every grade` `, done on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `section 3 prohibits the work` (`a holder of a` `grade 2` `licence granted on` (YMD 2026 10 1)) (`work on` `a 20 kW system on a non-flammable refrigerant` `that the First Schedule sets against` `every grade` `, done on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
-- Work the First Schedule sets only against a grade 3 licence.
#ASSERT `section 3 prohibits the work` (`a holder of a` `grade 2` `licence granted on` (YMD 2026 10 1)) (`work on` `a 20 kW system on a non-flammable refrigerant` `that the First Schedule sets against` (LIST `grade 3`) `, done on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
-- A licence granted 1.4.2026 lasts to 31.3.2031; on 1.4.2031 it has lapsed.
#ASSERT NOT `section 3 prohibits the work` (`a holder of a` `grade 3` `licence granted on` (YMD 2026 4 1)) (`work on` `a 20 kW system on a non-flammable refrigerant` `that the First Schedule sets against` `every grade` `, done on` (YMD 2031 3 31)) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT `section 3 prohibits the work` (`a holder of a` `grade 3` `licence granted on` (YMD 2026 4 1)) (`work on` `a 20 kW system on a non-flammable refrigerant` `that the First Schedule sets against` `every grade` `, done on` (YMD 2031 4 1)) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
-- The fifth anniversary is inside the validity period (Interpretation Law
-- s 10(b)): the holder of a licence granted 15.2.2025 may still work on
-- Friday 15.2.2030, and not on Saturday 16.2.2030, unless Fridays and
-- Saturdays are rest days, when the licence runs to Sunday 17.2.2030 (s 10(c)).
#ASSERT NOT `section 3 prohibits the work` (`a holder of a` `grade 3` `licence granted on` (YMD 2025 2 15)) (`work on` `a 20 kW system on a non-flammable refrigerant` `that the First Schedule sets against` `every grade` `, done on` (YMD 2030 2 15)) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT `section 3 prohibits the work` (`a holder of a` `grade 3` `licence granted on` (YMD 2025 2 15)) (`work on` `a 20 kW system on a non-flammable refrigerant` `that the First Schedule sets against` `every grade` `, done on` (YMD 2030 2 16)) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `section 3 prohibits the work` (`a holder of a` `grade 3` `licence granted on` (YMD 2025 2 15)) (`work on` `a 20 kW system on a non-flammable refrigerant` `that the First Schedule sets against` `every grade` `, done on` (YMD 2030 2 16)) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest`
#ASSERT `section 3 prohibits the work` (`a holder of a` `grade 3` `licence granted on` (YMD 2025 2 15)) (`work on` `a 20 kW system on a non-flammable refrigerant` `that the First Schedule sets against` `every grade` `, done on` (YMD 2030 2 18)) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest`
-- An order under s. 3(b).
#ASSERT NOT `section 3 prohibits the work` `a person with no licence` (`work on` `a 10 kW system of a type exempted by order` `that the First Schedule sets against` `every grade` `, done on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`

-- The prohibition, traced: unlicensed work done on day 5 → BREACH.
#TRACE `section 3(a) — the duty not to do the work unlicensed` `a person with no licence` (`work on` `a 10 kW split system on a non-flammable refrigerant` `that the First Schedule sets against` `every grade` `, done on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person doing the work` DOES `do work on the refrigeration or air-conditioning system` AT 5

§§ `Section 16 — updating particulars`

-- Interpretation Law s 10(a): the day of the change is not counted, so the
-- thirtieth day after it is the last day. Change on Monday 1.3.2027: last day
-- Wednesday 31.3.2027 (unchanged by the correction).
GIVEN `the change` IS A DATE
      `the notice` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Change of particulars`
`a change on` `the change` `, notified on` `the notice` MEANS
    `Change of particulars` WITH `the day of the change` IS `the change`, `the day the Registrar was notified` IS `the notice`

#ASSERT `section 16 — the last day for notifying the Registrar of` (`a change on` (YMD 2027 3 1) `, notified on` NOTHING) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2027 3 31
#ASSERT `section 16 — the Registrar was notified in time of` (`a change on` (YMD 2027 3 1) `, notified on` (JUST (YMD 2027 3 31))) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `section 16 — the Registrar was notified in time of` (`a change on` (YMD 2027 3 1) `, notified on` (JUST (YMD 2027 4 1))) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `section 16 — the Registrar was notified in time of` (`a change on` (YMD 2027 3 1) `, notified on` NOTHING) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`

-- s 10(c), applied to a deadline (fork F31). Change on Thursday 4.3.2027: the
-- thirtieth day is Saturday 3.4.2027. With no rest days a notice on Sunday
-- 4.4.2027 is late; with Saturdays, or Fridays and Saturdays, as rest days the
-- period runs to Sunday 4.4.2027 and the notice is in time; Monday 5.4.2027 is
-- late either way.
#ASSERT `section 16 — the last day for notifying the Registrar of` (`a change on` (YMD 2027 3 4) `, notified on` NOTHING) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 3
#ASSERT `section 16 — the last day for notifying the Registrar of` (`a change on` (YMD 2027 3 4) `, notified on` NOTHING) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 4
#ASSERT NOT `section 16 — the Registrar was notified in time of` (`a change on` (YMD 2027 3 4) `, notified on` (JUST (YMD 2027 4 4))) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT `section 16 — the Registrar was notified in time of` (`a change on` (YMD 2027 3 4) `, notified on` (JUST (YMD 2027 4 4))) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest`
#ASSERT `section 16 — the Registrar was notified in time of` (`a change on` (YMD 2027 3 4) `, notified on` (JUST (YMD 2027 4 4))) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `section 16 — the Registrar was notified in time of` (`a change on` (YMD 2027 3 4) `, notified on` (JUST (YMD 2027 4 5))) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest`
-- Two rest days in a row at the end (the Interpretation row's fork F3, its
-- reading A: the period runs on to the first day that is not a rest day).
-- Change on Wednesday 3.3.2027: the thirtieth day is Friday 2.4.2027. With
-- Saturdays only, Friday is a working day and the period ends that Friday; with
-- Fridays and Saturdays, Friday 2 and Saturday 3 are both rest days and it ends
-- on Sunday 4.4.2027.
#ASSERT NOT `section 16 — the Registrar was notified in time of` (`a change on` (YMD 2027 3 3) `, notified on` (JUST (YMD 2027 4 4))) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest`
#ASSERT `section 16 — the Registrar was notified in time of` (`a change on` (YMD 2027 3 3) `, notified on` (JUST (YMD 2027 4 4))) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest`

-- The duty, traced on a timeline whose day 0 is the day of the change.
-- Change 1.3.2027, no rest days: day 30 is in time, day 31 is late.
#TRACE `section 16 — the licence holder shall notify the Registrar of` (`a change on` (YMD 2027 3 1) `, notified on` NOTHING) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licence holder` DOES `notify the Registrar of the change in particulars` AT 30
#TRACE `section 16 — the licence holder shall notify the Registrar of` (`a change on` (YMD 2027 3 1) `, notified on` NOTHING) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licence holder` DOES `notify the Registrar of the change in particulars` AT 31
-- Change 4.3.2027, Saturdays as rest days: day 31 (Sunday 4.4.2027) is in time.
#TRACE `section 16 — the licence holder shall notify the Registrar of` (`a change on` (YMD 2027 3 4) `, notified on` NOTHING) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licence holder` DOES `notify the Registrar of the change in particulars` AT 31

§§ `Section 17 — continuing training`

GIVEN d IS A DATE, h IS A NUMBER, ok IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Course attended`
`a course on` d `of` h `hours, requirements met:` ok MEANS
    `Course attended` WITH
        `the day attended`                                              IS d
        `hours`                                                         IS h
        `under the supervision of the Ministry`                         IS TRUE
        `conducted by the Registrar or recognised by the Division`      IS TRUE
        `in the field of the holder's work under the licence`           IS TRUE
        `on a date the Registrar directed`                              IS TRUE
        `the holder met the course's requirements`                      IS ok

-- A licence whose validity ends 31.3.2030: its last year is 1.4.2029 to
-- 31.3.2030, 365 days.
#ASSERT `section 17(a) — the number of days in the last year of validity ending on` (YMD 2030 3 31) EQUALS 365
#ASSERT `section 17(a) — the duty is met, for a licence whose validity ends on` (YMD 2030 3 31) (LIST `a course on` (YMD 2029 6 1) `of` 4 `hours, requirements met:` TRUE, `a course on` (YMD 2030 2 1) `of` 4 `hours, requirements met:` TRUE)
-- Seven hours is not eight.
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(a) — the duty is met, for a licence whose validity ends on` (YMD 2030 3 31) (LIST `a course on` (YMD 2029 6 1) `of` 4 `hours, requirements met:` TRUE, `a course on` (YMD 2030 2 1) `of` 3 `hours, requirements met:` TRUE)
-- A course on 31.3.2029 is before the last year began.
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(a) — the duty is met, for a licence whose validity ends on` (YMD 2030 3 31) (LIST `a course on` (YMD 2029 3 31) `of` 4 `hours, requirements met:` TRUE, `a course on` (YMD 2030 2 1) `of` 4 `hours, requirements met:` TRUE)
#ASSERT `section 17(a) — the duty is met, for a licence whose validity ends on` (YMD 2030 3 31) (LIST `a course on` (YMD 2029 4 1) `of` 4 `hours, requirements met:` TRUE, `a course on` (YMD 2030 3 31) `of` 4 `hours, requirements met:` TRUE)
-- "ויעמוד בדרישות אותן השתלמויות": a course whose requirements were not met
-- does not count.
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(a) — the duty is met, for a licence whose validity ends on` (YMD 2030 3 31) (LIST `a course on` (YMD 2029 6 1) `of` 8 `hours, requirements met:` FALSE)

-- (ג) at most three months: by Interpretation Law s 10(b), three months after
-- 31.3.2030 end on 30.6.2030, June having no 31st (unchanged by the correction).
#ASSERT `section 17(c) — the extension is within the Registrar's power` WITH `the last day of validity` IS YMD 2030 3 31, `the extended last day` IS YMD 2030 6 30, `the holder did not meet the duty under (a) or (b)` IS TRUE, `the Registrar consulted the Council` IS TRUE, `the Registrar found a special case and justified circumstances` IS TRUE, `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS `no days of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(c) — the extension is within the Registrar's power` WITH `the last day of validity` IS YMD 2030 3 31, `the extended last day` IS YMD 2030 7 1, `the holder did not meet the duty under (a) or (b)` IS TRUE, `the Registrar consulted the Council` IS TRUE, `the Registrar found a special case and justified circumstances` IS TRUE, `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS `no days of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(c) — the extension is within the Registrar's power` WITH `the last day of validity` IS YMD 2030 3 31, `the extended last day` IS YMD 2030 6 30, `the holder did not meet the duty under (a) or (b)` IS TRUE, `the Registrar consulted the Council` IS TRUE, `the Registrar found a special case and justified circumstances` IS FALSE, `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS `no days of rest`
-- s 10(c), applied to the extension, a period for doing something (fork F31).
-- Validity ending Friday 29.3.2030: three months later is Saturday 29.6.2030.
-- With no rest days an extension to Sunday 30.6.2030 is too long; with
-- Saturdays, or Fridays and Saturdays, as rest days it is within the power.
-- An extension to Monday 1.7.2030 is too long either way.
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(c) — the extension is within the Registrar's power` WITH `the last day of validity` IS YMD 2030 3 29, `the extended last day` IS YMD 2030 6 30, `the holder did not meet the duty under (a) or (b)` IS TRUE, `the Registrar consulted the Council` IS TRUE, `the Registrar found a special case and justified circumstances` IS TRUE, `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS `no days of rest`
#ASSERT `section 17(c) — the extension is within the Registrar's power` WITH `the last day of validity` IS YMD 2030 3 29, `the extended last day` IS YMD 2030 6 30, `the holder did not meet the duty under (a) or (b)` IS TRUE, `the Registrar consulted the Council` IS TRUE, `the Registrar found a special case and justified circumstances` IS TRUE, `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS `Saturdays are days of rest`
#ASSERT `section 17(c) — the extension is within the Registrar's power` WITH `the last day of validity` IS YMD 2030 3 29, `the extended last day` IS YMD 2030 6 30, `the holder did not meet the duty under (a) or (b)` IS TRUE, `the Registrar consulted the Council` IS TRUE, `the Registrar found a special case and justified circumstances` IS TRUE, `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS `Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(c) — the extension is within the Registrar's power` WITH `the last day of validity` IS YMD 2030 3 29, `the extended last day` IS YMD 2030 7 1, `the holder did not meet the duty under (a) or (b)` IS TRUE, `the Registrar consulted the Council` IS TRUE, `the Registrar found a special case and justified circumstances` IS TRUE, `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS `Saturdays are days of rest`

-- (ב).
#ASSERT `section 17(b) — the Registrar may require the holder to take part in this course` WITH `the course was conducted by the Registrar or recognised by the Division after consulting the Council` IS TRUE, `the Registrar found circumstances that justify it` IS TRUE, `the Registrar found the course needed for the holder's training and for the purposes of this Law` IS TRUE, `notice was given a reasonable time before the course` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(b) — the Registrar may require the holder to take part in this course` WITH `the course was conducted by the Registrar or recognised by the Division after consulting the Council` IS TRUE, `the Registrar found circumstances that justify it` IS TRUE, `the Registrar found the course needed for the holder's training and for the purposes of this Law` IS TRUE, `notice was given a reasonable time before the course` IS FALSE

-- (ד).
#ASSERT `section 17(d) — taking part in the courses and meeting their requirements is deemed a condition of the licence`

-- (א) traced on its own timeline: courses completed on day 200 → FULFILLED;
-- nothing by day 366 → BREACH.
#TRACE `section 17(a) — the licence holder shall take part in continuing training` (YMD 2030 3 31) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licence holder` DOES `take part in at least eight hours of continuing-training courses` AT 200
#TRACE `section 17(a) — the licence holder shall take part in continuing training` (YMD 2030 3 31) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 366)
